  "id": "DrugBank_DB05266 - MONDO_4765",
  "verbalization": "Ibudilast is implicated in the pathogenesis of Intrinsic Asthma through a series of indirect but interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Ibudilast is associated with Asthma, which in turn is linked to Intrinsic Asthma via different mediators. Specifically, Ibudilast is indicated for Asthma, and Asthma is indicated for Fluticasone Furoate and Nedocromil, both of which are known to contribute to the development of Intrinsic Asthma. This implies that Ibudilast may exert a modulatory effect on the inflammatory processes that underlie Intrinsic Asthma, potentially through the activation of bronchodilatory pathways or anti-inflammatory mechanisms. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Ibudilast to Intrinsic Asthma highlights the complexity of the relationship, suggesting that Ibudilast may act as a secondary mediator in the progression of Asthma to Intrinsic Asthma. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering the broader pharmacological and physiological context in assessing the potential repositioning of Ibudilast for use in Intrinsic Asthma.",
